    "message": "A class a reopened Object's body makes is named as a top-level one\n\nclass_ruby_name builds a class's Ruby name from its enclosing classes, and\na reopened Object was one of them, so `class Object; B = Class.new;\nS = Struct.new(:a); M2 = Module.new; end` named them Object::B,\nObject::S and Object::M2, where CRuby names Object's constants as the\ntop level's: B, S, M2. The walk now stops at Object. Only the identity\nkey of an anonymous class made there changes in the corpus C.\n\nFound while checking CodeRabbit's notes on PR #10774; master named them\nso too.\n\nRefs #10774\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <[redacted-email]>",
